course: dictionary
lesson: 15603
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Tameness is one of them. Read the words around it to find out which meaning the writer means. «The tameness of the deer let the hikers walk right up to it.» The deer is gentle and not afraid of people, so tameness means being tame.
explain: Now look at this sentence: «The tameness of the film made the audience yawn.» A film cannot be tame like an animal. The yawning is the clue: the film was dull and not exciting enough. So here tameness means being mild and dull.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. Does "the gentleness of the film" make sense? No. Does "the dullness of the film" make sense? Yes. Choose the meaning that fits.
fact: Tameness is a noun. It names the quality of being tame.
fact: Tame means gentle, used to people and not afraid of them, so tameness is how tame an animal is.
fact: «The parrot's tameness showed that it had lived with people for years.»
fact: «The tameness of the birds» on a remote island can show they have never learned to fear people.
fact: Tameness can also mean being dull or mild, like a boring film. Tameness is uncountable, so we say "great tameness", not "two tamenesses".
exercise: «The tameness of the deer let the hikers walk right up to it.» What does tameness mean here? | *The deer was gentle and not afraid of people | The deer was very big and heavy | The deer was lost in the woods | The deer was wild and ran away fast
exercise: «The tameness of the film made the audience yawn.» What does tameness mean here? | The film had too many songs | The film was too frightening | The film was in a foreign language | *The film was dull and not exciting enough
exercise: Tameness is which part of speech? | *A noun | An adjective | An adverb | A verb
test: «The parrot's tameness showed it had lived with people for years.» What does tameness show? | It is about to fall asleep | *It is used to people and not afraid of them | It has a bad temper | It can fly very high
test: «The tameness of the birds on the remote island surprised the visitors.» Which word could replace tameness? | *Gentleness | Loudness | Speed | Colour
exam: «The tameness of the show left the children bored, as nothing exciting ever happened.» What does tameness mean here? | *Being dull, mild and not exciting enough | Being gentle and kind to people | Being afraid of everything | Being very loud and noisy
